<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konstantin Dragaš</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1395">1395</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Konstantin Dejanović</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konstantin Dragaš was a Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> who with his brother Jovan ruled a lordship in north-eastern Macedonia, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumanovo">Kumanovo</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyustendil">Velbazhd</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strumica">Strumica</a>, after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a>. He became an Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> and was killed fighting for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rovine">Battle of Rovine</a> in 1395. His daughter Helena married Manuel II and was the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-xi-palaiologos">Constantine XI</a>, the last Byzantine emperor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konstantin-dragas.jpg" alt="Konstantin Dragaš" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RunnerTrees · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SerbianMagnateKonstantinDragasDejanovic.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
